<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 63,890 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 63,890 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 63,890 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Thursday compared to 62,240 tonnes in the same period on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>						Thursday    September 4</p>
<p>    Export cargo			   8,924	8,752</p>
<p>    Import cargo			  54,966     53,488</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, seven ships sailed and three berthed. In the next 24 hours, four were expected to sail and eight were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Crude oil		70,000	 Capt Miranda	  6/9</p>
<p>Gas oil		  44,000	 Keefan		  6/9</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 42,000	 Zagara		  7/9</p>
<p>Sugar		    13,543	 Rong Jiang	    7/9</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     19,630	 Mitera Vassiliki    7/9</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     31,500	 Maria Topic	   8/9</p>
<p>Sugar		     7,500	 Mehedinti	    10/9</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
